  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SOCWE Alternative Youth Skills Training and Employment Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sector: Youth skills training and job placement. Beneficiaries: 200 youth, of whom 110 are women. Summary: This project will provide marketable skills training for 200 youth in Mogadishu over two years. Beneficiaries will be trained in: journalism, secretarial skills, welding, electricity, and tailoring and tie-dye clothing production. SOCWE aims to help 75% of the trained youth secure employment, while the other 25% will be supported in starting their own businesses.</narrative>
  </description>
